  "description": "The tail's two blocks act on different terms, so their steps commute and MultiStepReduction fixes no order beyond each step's redex being present. Running block 2 BEFORE block 1 -- the reverse of the engine's deg-lex schedule -- means block 2's bystander is term 1 in its PRE-block form, which is not an extension of the block's left context. Measured: under the reordered schedule [block2, block1, monic, monic] BOTH hpark hypotheses hold, every step's source is unique in the term list (monicStep's hne), and the chain still reaches zero. So the collision hecke-tail-collision-check found is a scheduling artifact: nothing needs weakening, the tail assembles from the lemmas already on main.",
